# The packages of the image's live system (ci/build-image.sh), beside what
# mmdebstrap's "standard" variant gives, which is what the Debian installer
# gives with "standard system utilities" ticked. The live system is the
# system the installer copies to the disk: everything a Kidux machine has,
# and what installs it, which the installer takes off again (kidux-installer).
#
# Kidux, as the user guide installs it on Debian: its archive and key, and
# kidux-base, with its recommends.
kidux-archive-keyring
kidux-apt-source
kidux-base
# The kernel, and the administrator's sudo and console the Debian installer
# gives.
linux-image-amd64
sudo
keyboard-configuration
console-setup
# Booting: the live system from the image, and GRUB on the disk for either
# way a computer starts. grub-efi-amd64 comes with the signed GRUB and the
# shim, for Secure Boot; a computer that starts with a BIOS gets grub-pc in
# its place from the image's pool/ (kidux-installer-grub).
live-boot
grub-efi-amd64
grub-efi-amd64-signed
shim-signed
grub-pc-bin
efibootmgr
# The installer.
kidux-installer
